            <ArticleTitle>Physiology of the placebo effect, and the evidence for changes in brain metabolism.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>54-60</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Placebo effects are accompanied by localised changes in brain physiology. Variation between individuals in the extent of a placebo effect is due to genetic variation in brain enzyme activity. Some of the effect of any active drug is a placebo effect, and this should be considered in the evaluation of overall action.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
